    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math fascinating, especially in physics and its real-world applications. Though I didn’t pursue it deeply in school, my master’s in physics gave me a solid foundation. I see math as a language of patterns and logic—something I appreciate in cooking, yoga, and even birdwatching. It’s not my favorite subject, but I respect its structure and elegance.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not usually, but I do feel a bit of tension when faced with complex equations or unfamiliar concepts. That anxiety often comes from not knowing the steps, not from the math itself. I’ve learned to approach it calmly, like a yoga session—breathe, focus, and take it one step at a time. My background in physics helps me see math as a tool, not a barrier.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used AI tools like chatbots and math tutors to review calculus concepts. I found them helpful for quick explanations and step-by-step solutions. They made abstract ideas more tangible, especially when I was preparing for a workshop on physics applications. The experience was positive—clear, patient, and accessible—though I still preferred human guidance for deeper understanding.",
