    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and generate step-by-step solutions tailored to individual learning styles. They can adapt to students’ pace, provide instant feedback, and help visualize abstract ideas. In classrooms, they could support teachers by generating practice problems or explaining difficult topics. This makes math more accessible, especially for students who struggle with traditional methods."
